        "original_id": "5275adf3-a68a-5a08-a932-c2f02c55ef4d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Lovell, Jeffrey Kluger\n- Products: Lost Moon, Apollo 13\n- Organizations: NASA, United States Navy\n- Events: Apollo 13 mission, April 1970 Apollo 13 lunar landing mission\n- Roles: astronaut, journalist, mission commander, captain\n\nFacts:\n- In April 1970, the Apollo 13 lunar landing mission failed en route to the Moon, and the crew returned safely to Earth with help from mission control.\n- James Arthur Lovell Jr. was born on March 25, 1928.\n- James Lovell is a former NASA astronaut and a retired captain in the United States Navy.\n- James Lovell commanded the Apollo 13 mission and is most famous for that role.\n- In 1994, astronaut James Lovell and journalist Jeffrey Kluger first published the non-fiction book Lost Moon.\n- Lost Moon was published in paperback as Apollo 13.\n- Lost Moon is about the failed April 1970 Apollo 13 lunar landing mission.",
